<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1465–1524</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez">Diego Velázquez</a> de Cuéllar was a Spanish conquistador who led the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> from 1511 and became its first governor. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baracoa">Baracoa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de Cuba and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hatuey">Hatuey</a>, who resisted, was burnt in 1512. In 1519 he sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> but failed to stop him acting on his own account.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez-de-cuellar.jpg" alt="Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DiegoVelazquezCuellar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
